    "body": "Ropes → Update clipboard when switching ropes On by default. Switching to a nonempty collecting rope copies its first card to the clipboard for your next manual paste. Cards → Update clipboard when the first card changes On by default. When you rearrange the current collecting rope and a different card becomes first, its contents are copied. Saving an edit to the first card’s text also updates the clipboard. Scrolling through cards, canceling a drag or switching to an empty rope leaves the clipboard as it was. Neither setting sends a paste shortcut to another window. Ropes → Capacity for new ropes sets the starting limit for ropes you create later. The default is 100; enter a whole number of at least 1. This does not trim existing ropes. To change one, use its Edit style… command."
