    "body": "Open Storage & Privacy → Clipboard capture exclusions and choose Edit list…. Enter the app’s executable name, such as KeePass.exe, and choose Add. Enter the filename without its folder path. Choose Save. Future copies from the listed apps are skipped. Cards already in your history stay there. Add up to 64 executable names of at most 255 characters each. Names are case-insensitive; paths, wildcards and duplicates are rejected. If Save reports a pending name, click Add or clear the input first. Closing the editor discards unsaved list changes. ClipRope also honors Windows privacy flags on each copy, even for apps outside the list. It skips a copy if the app supplies ExcludeClipboardContentFromMonitorProcessing, or supplies CanIncludeInClipboardHistory with a value other than 1. A flag that only blocks cloud sync still allows local capture. To skip every copy from an app, add its executable to the list."
